==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|NL.}} {{term|paraplegia|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|lang=grc|παραπληγία}}, Ionic Greek for {{term|lang=grc|παραπληξία||paralysis on one side}}, from {{term|lang=grc|παραπλήσσεσθαι||to be stricken on one side}}, active {{term|lang=grc|παραπλήσσειν||to strike on one side}}, from {{term|lang=grc|παρά||beside}} + {{term|lang=grc|πλήσσειν||to strike}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{pathology}} A [[condition]] where the lower half of a patient's body is [[paralyzed]] and cannot move.

====Related terms====
* [[monoplegia]]
* [[hemiplegia]]
* [[paraplegic]]
* [[quadriplegia]]

